"1912","On the authority of Al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, who said: Abu Bakr came asking permission to enter upon the Prophet (peace be upon him). He heard Aisha raising her voice at the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him). He was given permission and entered, and said: ""O daughter of Umm Ruman!"" And he seized her, saying: ""Do you raise your voice at the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)?"" The Prophet (peace be upon him) interposed between him and her. When Abu Bakr left, the Prophet (peace be upon him) began saying to her, appeasing her: ""Do you not see that I have interposed between the man and you?"" Then Abu Bakr came again and asked permission to enter, and found him laughing with her. He was given permission and entered, and Abu Bakr said to him: ""O Messenger of Allah, include me in your peace as you included me in your war."""
"1913",""
"1914",""
"1915","On the authority of ʿĀmir, who said: I heard al-Nuʿmān ibn Bashīr delivering a sermon on the pulpit, and he said: “My father gave me a gift. ʿAmra bint Rawāḥa said: ‘I will not be pleased until you have the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) witness it.’ So Bashīr came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) and said: ‘I have given my son a gift.’ ʿAmra bint Rawāḥa said: ‘I will not be pleased until the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) witnesses it.’ He said: ‘Do you have other children besides him?’ He said: ‘Yes.’ He said: ‘Have you given all of them the like of what you gave him?’ He said: ‘No.’ He said: ‘This is injustice; so do not ask me to witness it. Fear Allah and treat your children justly, just as you would like them to be dutiful to you.’”"
