"2021","On the authority of Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, who said: When the matter of Uthman ibn Maz'un arose — who had been abstaining from women — the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent for him and said: ""O Uthman! I have not been commanded to practice monasticism. Have you turned away from my Sunnah?"" He said: ""No, O Messenger of Allah."" He said: ""Indeed, part of my Sunnah is that I pray and sleep, fast and break my fast, marry women and divorce them. So whoever turns away from my Sunnah is not of me. O Uthman! Verily, your family has a right over you, and your eye has a right over you."" Sa'd said: ""By Allah, there were men among the Muslims who had agreed that if the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had allowed Uthman to continue as he was, they would have castrated themselves and become celibate."""
"2022",""
